A||N||3||soup||Few questions, please help (stereo, and new fascia)||||5||
Z||000000||soup||11-11-2001||05:56 AM||||Hi, I want to add an aftermarket Fasica, ive read on here about an MR2 Shogun front bumper, I like the look of it, but how would I go about adding this to my 87 GT. I want the type of bumper with the "teeth" pointing out, something like a VS Combat, Razzi, or that Shogun for an MR2. Any information would be helpfull. <P>Also, I had a stereo in my old crappy 84 LeBaron convertable, it is 3 JL W3 10", running off of a Zapco 750. I want to be able to put at least one in my Fiero. I want to build a box to fit between the passenger seat and the firewall using 1/2" MDF, has anyone done this with a 10"? I did a loose mesurement and I think I only have about 4 inches for the depth of the sub. I hope i can do it and still be able to put the seat all the way back. Once again, any information on this would be very helpfull. Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-11-2001||06:04 AM||||The Shogun front fascia won't work unless you modify it.  There are a million kits out there and about as many body mods you can purchase.<P>fierosound put a 10" sub behind each seat.  The Fiero has a double rear firewall so, if you cut out the right place (just about big enough for the magnet) you can gain a couple inches.  I don't remember the URL to his site, but someone will come up with it.  You can also build a ported bandpass box for the front compartment (this is what I'm doing).  Click <A HREF="http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark" TARGET=_blank>here</A>.<P>Welcome to the club.||||reg||1
Z||000002||soup||11-12-2001||03:20 AM||||Thanks!<P>I read on the net last night about a person who put 2 10" behind his seats and cut out the fire wall, he won a few awards for his install, im not sure if this is FieroSound or not but I am a little worried about cutting into the firewall, also I would think sealing the box would be a little difficult.<P>That is an awesome dash on your site! I take it you did that yourself? Where would I be able to find an aftermarket dash similar to that. I saw one at V8 Archies, but I havent been able to see exactly what it looks like.<P>Also I have been looking everywhere but I cant seem to find any aftermarket font fascias. All I can seem to find is spoilers and full body kits. Do you know of an actual webpage where I can go to find some aftermarket fascias? <P>Im only 17 and I just bought this car, its my first car and I still have money left over on my loan, so im hoping i can find one for around $300 USD max, and as soon as possible.<P>Any leads would be greatly appriciated!<BR>Thanks again!||||reg||10
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-12-2001||09:10 AM||||That's not my site nor is it my dash.  Wish I had the talent for that.  The guys name is Brian.  He's been on the forum before, but he's not a regular member.||||reg||1
